feat(panel/proxy): hands-off agent output review + compile/PDF proxy hardening

Field round: the user could open projects but the assist panel was unusable
(covered by the fixed iframe) and the editor still stalled on Loading.

- view.tsx: when the assist panel opens, the persistent iframe yields its
  right-side width (panel is painted above the root-context frame), so all
  panel controls are clickable.
- agent output flow hardened: the fixed workspace handoff file is polled
  for a STABLE revision (two consecutive identical polls + mtime signature),
  cleaned of one outer latex/tex fence, and placed into the reviewable
  custom-content box — the user inspects and clicks "Insert at caret"
  (no blind insertion into the editor).
- waiting UI: spinner + live wait seconds + cancel; 10-minute timeout.
- routeUrl: absolute same-origin URLs (window.origin + file.url built by
  the compile result builder) are re-rooted under the proxy, including
  Request objects; dynamic resource attributes share the same routing.
- proxy: synchronous compile calls get a 10-minute timeout; relative
  upstream redirects resolve against the full request URL (project-scoped
  PDF downloads).
- smoke: compile + ranged-PDF regression; panel-width and output-flow
  assertions; bridge routing-form assertions.
- version 0.3.5.
